<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Concurrency - Tag - loommii</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/tags/concurrency/</link><description>我的个人技术博客</description><generator>Hugo 0.165.0 &amp; FixIt v0.4.5</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 16 Jan 2026 01:28:43 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://loommii.github.io/en/tags/concurrency/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Go: Channel Might Lead to Goroutine Leaks</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/posts/channel_may_cause_goroutine_leak/</link><pubDate>Fri, 07 Mar 2025 14:12:02 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/posts/channel_may_cause_goroutine_leak/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/techarticle/">TechArticle</category><description>Detailed explanation of why Channels in Go might cause Goroutine leaks and their solutions.</description></item><item><title>Locks</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/posts/locks/</link><pubDate>Sun, 08 Dec 2024 00:28:39 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/posts/locks/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/techarticle/">TechArticle</category><description>&lt;p&gt;In concurrent computing, computers are highly likely to encounter data corruption issues. Therefore, &amp;ldquo;locks&amp;rdquo; are introduced to solve this type of problem.&#10;Common locks: Mutex, Spinlock, Read-Write Lock, Pessimistic Lock, Optimistic Lock.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Processes, Threads, and Coroutines</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/posts/processes_threads_coroutines/</link><pubDate>Sun, 08 Dec 2024 00:28:02 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/posts/processes_threads_coroutines/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/techarticle/">TechArticle</category><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;In terms of computer architecture, these concepts range from largest to smallest: &lt;code&gt;Program -&amp;gt; Process -&amp;gt; Thread -&amp;gt; Coroutine&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;</description></item><item><title>Go Daily Question 039</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_039/</link><pubDate>Fri, 06 Dec 2024 20:44:16 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_039/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;Regarding channels, which of the following syntax is correct:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;A. var ch chan int&#10;B. ch := make(chan int)&#10;C. &amp;lt;- ch&#10;D. ch &amp;lt;-&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;Answer: ABC&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;A and B both declare a channel; C reads from a channel;&#10;Writing to a channel must include a value, so D is incorrect.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/details&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>